{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1198 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "a18d6c4170a16b94527e1ac55e8c6c7f622f5148b782832f15fd12d233465ec3" :edb/db-before-t 1197 :edb/db-after-t 1198 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534510 50 #inst "2026-10-12T01:26:06.891Z" 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186133579 1071 "If ![](images/16/16e82b08842bdec1de657e14110b08037cca4452d1f0e8c64a8fd783037adeb6.png) and ![](images/55/559785dc3071ba5018f9b97d45e18e9f7bf937f702f9eeaf0a9c5ae087d5b43f.png) are orthogonal vectors, find the value of $k.$" 13194139534510 17592186045417 false] [17592186133579 1071 "If ![](images/55/55d5d5dc4af3eaf8d0bf0474fd77731242346be452c109d6bbc6fdb52033a647.svg) and ![](images/6d/6dc2b50d6bb8a7d2fcc50be918737857d065088320010a356c626e1417efcc82.svg) are orthogonal vectors, find the value of $k.$" 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186133580 1071 "Let ![](images/61/61cb89adc9a0cce6a434c41be5d2d1799e01e94bebe1b4f44d48bc011c1a349b.png) and ![](images/00/00af13e5017635a0b333ecd5fc2bfc761c9612427b8a3986ba48fa904ff2eed0.png) be vectors such that $\\mathbf{u} \\!\\perp\\! \\mathbf{w}$. Find $(\\mathbf{u}+\\mathbf{v})\\cdot \\mathbf{w} + \\mathbf{u}\\cdot(\\mathbf{v}+ \\mathbf{w}).$" 13194139534510 17592186045417 false] [17592186133580 1071 "Let ![](images/ae/ae5c0c967a0ddd28c163a51aca44edc3340cb76a2f9da28704563b423c591de8.svg) and ![](images/9a/9afd33bf9d62d13ceab462ed9705c007173253b065b347c6475acbff5b8090fe.svg) be vectors such that $\\mathbf{u} \\!\\perp\\! \\mathbf{w}$. Find $(\\mathbf{u}+\\mathbf{v})\\cdot \\mathbf{w} + \\mathbf{u}\\cdot(\\mathbf{v}+ \\mathbf{w}).$" 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186133581 1071 "Let ![](images/1f/1fb7970633bab3a0518872b1eb14dcfdef5c95f1b6bc01760f4cff1680350413.svg) and ![](images/a1/a1a509e6431cd3b3625d4960bdcd10106da3b60a9d7f7bc9dd11089a6b8960b2.svg) be vectors such that $\\mathbf{u}$ is orthogonal to $\\mathbf{v}$ and $\\mathbf{w}$. What is the value of $a+b?$" 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186133581 1071 "Let ![](images/61/618da6573504088a90064c503b3603f9c1cbedaee493473db435765ca635bdb9.png) and ![](images/a7/a71f47b53dab435e794fa5c4c889141b8ce32c93715abd56e0dc48d6535865b8.png) be vectors such that $\\mathbf{u}$ is orthogonal to $\\mathbf{v}$ and $\\mathbf{w}$. What is the value of $a+b?$" 13194139534510 17592186045417 false] [17592186133581 1074 "Given that $\\mathbf{u}$ is orthogonal to $\\mathbf{v}$ and $\\mathbf{w}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v=0 \\\\ u\\cdot w=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's consider the first equation $\\mathbf{u}\\cdot\\mathbf{v}=0$. Calculating the dot product in terms of $a$ and $b$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & =0 \\\\ -8\\cdot 6+a\\cdot (-15)+b\\cdot 9+(-10)\\cdot (-12) & =0 \\\\ -48-15a+9b+120 & =0 \\\\ -15a+9b & =-72 \\\\ -5a+3b & =-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, for the second equation $\\mathbf{u}\\cdot\\mathbf{w}=0$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot w & =0 \\\\ -8\\cdot 4+a\\cdot 2+b\\cdot (-5)+(-10)\\cdot (-3) & =0 \\\\ -32+2a-5b+30 & =0 \\\\ 2a-5b & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to find the values of $a$ and $b$, we need to solve the system\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}-5a+3b=-24 \\\\ 2a-5b=2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $2$ and the second equation by $5$, we get\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-10a+6b=-48 \\\\ 10a-25b=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, adding the above equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n-19b = -38 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad b = 2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $b = 2$ into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a-5(2) & =2 \\\\ 2a-10 & =2 \\\\ 2a & =12 \\\\ a & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have that\n\n$$\na+b = 6 + 2 = 8.\n$$" 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186133581 1074 "Given that $\\mathbf{u}$ is orthogonal to $\\mathbf{v}$ and $\\mathbf{w}$, we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v=0 \\\\ u\\cdot w=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's consider the first equation $\\mathbf{u}\\cdot\\mathbf{v}=0$. Calculating the dot product in terms of $a$ and $b$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & =0 \\\\ -8\\cdot 6+a\\cdot (-15)+b\\cdot 9+(-10)\\cdot (-12) & =0 \\\\ -48-15a+9b+120 & =0 \\\\ -15a+9b & =-72 \\\\ -5a+3b & =-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, for the second equation $\\mathbf{u}\\cdot\\mathbf{w}=0$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot w & =0 \\\\ -8\\cdot 4+a\\cdot 2+b\\cdot (-5)+(-10)\\cdot (-3) & =0 \\\\ -32+2a-5b+30 & =0 \\\\ 2a-5b & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to find the values of $a$ and $b$, we need to solve the system\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-5a+3b=-24 \\\\ 2a-5b=2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $2$ and the second equation by $5$, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-10a+6b=-48 \\\\ 10a-25b=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, adding the above equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n-19b = -38 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad b = 2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $b = 2$ into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a-5(2) & =2 \\\\ 2a-10 & =2 \\\\ 2a & =12 \\\\ a & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have that\n\n$$\na+b = 6 + 2 = 8.\n$$" 13194139534510 17592186045417 false] [17592186133630 1071 "Given the vector ![](images/8f/8f1a6f36da1dacbd3e275372e06e9ff13e7f3600517066116f422d0f8cb00b47.svg), which of the following vectors are orthogonal to $\\mathbf{u}$?\n![](images/c9/c905bc151f6d6df0bfb610152baca3dfe0ff63c4789fa5377de31aa9996da61a.svg)" 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186133630 1071 "Given the vector ![](images/b8/b8e1e42d3c85f7b3783a0c46d5075e0c588f22a030f3d6a84da9ad3444ad35d0.png), which of the following vectors are orthogonal to $\\mathbf{u}$?\n![](images/6e/6e69c8002a518487ce4821efe1faae85ba7ec365b1bedf23d7bfcd30e10e42b5.png)" 13194139534510 17592186045417 false] [17592186133770 1038 #edb/ref 17592186423654 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186133771 1038 #edb/ref 17592186423652 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186133771 1038 #edb/ref 17592186423655 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186133772 1038 #edb/ref 17592186423656 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186133815 1038 #edb/ref 17592186423653 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186133986 1050 840.0 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186134252 1074 "Given that $u⊥v$ and $u⊥w$, we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v=0 \\\\ u\\cdot w=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's consider the first equation $u\\cdot v=0.$ Calculating the dot product in terms of $a$ and $b$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & =0 \\\\ -3\\cdot 3+a\\cdot 4+b\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 1 & =0 \\\\ -9+4a+b-4 & =0 \\\\ 4a+b & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, for the second equation $u\\cdot w=0$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot w & =0 \\\\ -3\\cdot 1+a\\cdot 1+b\\cdot (-3)-4\\cdot (-4) & =0 \\\\ -3+a-3b+16 & =0 \\\\ a-3b & =-13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to find the values of $a$ and $b$, we need to solve the system\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}4a+b=13 \\\\ a-3b=-13\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $3$ and adding the result to the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}13a=26\\,⟹\\,a=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=2$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(2)+b & =13 \\\\ 8+b & =13 \\\\ b & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have that\n\n$$\na+b=2+5=7.\n$$" 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186134252 1074 "Given that $u⊥v$ and $u⊥w$, we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v=0 \\\\ u\\cdot w=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's consider the first equation $u\\cdot v=0.$ Calculating the dot product in terms of $a$ and $b$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & =0 \\\\ -3\\cdot 3+a\\cdot 4+b\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 1 & =0 \\\\ -9+4a+b-4 & =0 \\\\ 4a+b & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, for the second equation $u\\cdot w=0$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot w & =0 \\\\ -3\\cdot 1+a\\cdot 1+b\\cdot (-3)-4\\cdot (-4) & =0 \\\\ -3+a-3b+16 & =0 \\\\ a-3b & =-13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to find the values of $a$ and $b$, we need to solve the system\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}4a+b=13 \\\\ a-3b=-13\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $3$ and adding the result to the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}13a=26\\,⟹\\,a=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=2$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(2)+b & =13 \\\\ 8+b & =13 \\\\ b & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have that\n\n$$\na+b=2+5=7.\n$$" 13194139534510 17592186045417 false] [17592186135037 1064 "Let $\\mathbf{u}$ and $\\mathbf{v}$ be vectors in $\\mathbb{R}^n$. What do we mean when we say that the vectors $\\mathbf{u}$ and $\\mathbf{v}$ are orthogonal?\n\nTwo vectors $\\mathbf{u}$ and $\\mathbf{v}$ are **orthogonal** if their dot product equals zero: \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u}\\cdot \\mathbf{v}=0\n$$\n\nIf two vectors are orthogonal, then we denote this by $\\mathbf{u} \\!\\perp\\! \\mathbf{v}$. For instance, the vectors \n\n![](images/29/29a81db4068e5bcc97fd38729ca19f11988a08e905bfc189e69c88357185ea31.svg)\n\nin $\\mathbb{R^2}$ are orthogonal, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}_{1}\\cdot {e}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =0+0 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** The zero vector $\\mathbf{0}$ is orthogonal to any vector $\\mathbf{u}\\in\\mathbb{R}^n$ since $\\mathbf{0}\\cdot\\mathbf{u}=0$." 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186135037 1064 "Let $\\mathbf{u}$ and $\\mathbf{v}$ be vectors in $\\mathbb{R}^n$. What do we mean when we say that the vectors $\\mathbf{u}$ and $\\mathbf{v}$ are orthogonal?\n\nTwo vectors $\\mathbf{u}$ and $\\mathbf{v}$ are **orthogonal** if their dot product equals zero: \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u}\\cdot \\mathbf{v}=0\n$$\n\nIf two vectors are orthogonal, then we denote this by $\\mathbf{u} \\!\\perp\\! \\mathbf{v}$. For instance, the vectors \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nin $\\mathbb{R^2}$ are orthogonal, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}_{1}\\cdot {e}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =0+0 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** The zero vector $\\mathbf{0}$ is orthogonal to any vector $\\mathbf{u}\\in\\mathbb{R}^n$ since $\\mathbf{0}\\cdot\\mathbf{u}=0$." 13194139534510 17592186045417 false] [17592186423622 1080 "5" 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186423622 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186423622 1083 #uuid "0126d44d-cbd6-5e5d-8f9b-fd5306980a4d" 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186423623 1080 "-70" 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186423623 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186423623 1083 #uuid "0ab9e3e6-5284-58be-a5fe-0054619d52b2" 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186423624 1080 "-3" 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186423624 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186423624 1083 #uuid "1602525e-bf2f-5fd3-827e-a1e276978ea0" 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186423625 1080 "$v$ and $x$ only" 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186423625 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186423625 1083 #uuid "1bfdcc5b-d056-5b31-b19a-05f23514f849" 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186423626 1080 "-37" 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186423626 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186423626 1083 #uuid "2349f6f7-0b4a-5590-8339-7329d0015da4" 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186423627 1080 "2" 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186423627 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186423627 1083 #uuid "2a702037-a4b0-50cc-97fd-b5d6788b58a7" 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186423628 1080 "-8" 13194139534510 17592186045417 true] [17592186423628 1082 #edb/ref 17